# At each n, there are edges e counted from 1 and vertices v forming an
# Euler path exactly when there are such edges f counted from 0: `rexxfrd2`
# with e the map j ↦ f(j − 1), which is a map into the edges, and every e is
# one, at f the map k ↦ e(k + 1). That map is f composed with the shift
# (`fcompt`), so `gtravsh` says the two paths are one.
